To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function. This function is used to terminate the program and return control to the operating system. Here is an example of how to use it:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(0);  // Terminate the program
    return 0;  // Return 0 to indicate successful program execution
}
